      "comment": "TUSCAN ROSE (8) ran a strong race on debut here over 1400m, showing good pace to lead but just run over late when beaten a neck. Can't see the drop back in trip being an issue given how sharp she looked there and with the added experience she should take plenty of beating. THERMIC (4) is a gelding by Toronado on debut for the Payne yard who has trialled nicely leading in. Billy Egan booked from a good draw and he should go well. VULCANA (9) is a nicely bred filly by Alabama Express for the Maher yard who has jumped out fairly well and should be respected. ROSE MILLA (7) is a So You Think filly for the Dabernig/Meech combination which is always worth keeping an eye on.",
